From a22bcc9bd1d51bebf3b8354a291790a4daa2bbb5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Guild-Idler Patch Tool <patch@guild-idler.local>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 09:17:26 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] 0224: Replayable Quest Chains -- data model foundation

Step (1) of the sequencing plan from patch 0223's rewritten Backlog
entry. Data model only -- no UI, no purchase logic, no resolution
logic yet.

New types: ChainReplayDifficulty (own union, not a reuse of
RaidDifficulty), ChainReplayDifficultyConfig, ActiveChainReplay
(deliberately not ActiveChain), ChainReplayResult, ChainReplayTierDef
(own type, not a reuse of UpgradeDef.unlocks).

New data/chainReplay.ts: CHAIN_REPLAY_DIFFICULTIES (Normal literal,
Heroic/Legendary tuning-backed, deliberately softer than raids' own
curve), CHAIN_REPLAY_TIERS (master unlock + all 6 saga bands, 29
chains mapped 1:1, verified by script), chainReplayTierForChain().

New persisted state: chainReplayTiersOwned/activeChainReplays on
GameState. SAVE_VERSION 46->47, migration 46 backfills both to empty
arrays. No eligibility backfill needed -- completedChains already
covers pre-existing clears.

13 new Tuning entries for difficulty config + the 7 gold costs.

Two minimal read-only query helpers on GuildManager:
hasChainReplayTier/isChainReplayEligible -- enforces master+band+
completedChains all required, confirmed design.

No UI changed, no engine action added, no existing behavior touched.

Verified: npx tsc --noEmit and npx vite build both pass clean.
Chain-to-band mapping verified by script: 29 ids, 29 unique, zero
duplicates, zero gaps. SAVE_VERSION chain contiguous (45->46->47), no
duplicate Tuning ids.
